    "format-version": "0.1",
    "license": "MIT",
    "release": "0.1",
    "name": "Split BAM by Path",
    "readme": "## What This Workflow Does\n\nThis workflow takes two input files:\n* **BAM file:** The main aligned sequence dataset.\n* **Path list file:** A text file containing target paths, or contigs (one per line).\n\n### Process\n1. **Splits the path list:** Breaks the input list into individual single-line text files.\n2. **Filters the BAM:** Parses the path/contig from each text file and extracts the matching reads from the main BAM file.\n3. **Generates individual BAMs:** Creates a collection of smaller, contig-specific BAM files.\n\nThis enables downstream tools to analyze individual contigs concurrently, significantly speeding up execution times.",
    "report": {
        "markdown": "\n# Workflow Execution Report\n\n## Workflow Inputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_inputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow Outputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_outputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow\n```galaxy\nworkflow_display()\n```\n"
    },
